---
import Docs from '../../layouts/Docs.astro';
import CodeBlock from '../../components/CodeBlock.astro';
import { ContextMenuColumns, ContextMenuFiles, ContextMenuPlayground } from '../../components/ContextMenuDemo';
---

<Docs
  title="Context Menu"
  description="Right-click and long-press menus with checkboxes, radio groups, submenus, and shortcuts."
>
  <h1 class="docs-title">Context Menu</h1>
  <p class="docs-lead">
    A menu that opens where the pointer is. Right-click a target, or long-press it on a touch screen. Use it for
    shortcuts to actions that are also reachable another way, such as a More button or a keyboard shortcut.
  </p>
  <div class="mt-8" id="context-menu-demo">
    <ContextMenuPlayground client:load />
  </div>
  <section class="prose-section">
    <h2 class="section-title">Usage</h2>
    <CodeBlock
      lang="tsx"
      title="Context menu usage"
      code={`import {
  ContextMenu,
  ContextMenuContent,
  ContextMenuGroup,
  ContextMenuItem,
  ContextMenuLabel,
  ContextMenuSeparator,
  ContextMenuShortcut,
  ContextMenuTrigger,
} from "@tulipfarm/sprout/context-menu";

<ContextMenu>
  <ContextMenuTrigger tabIndex={0} role="group" aria-label="Sample card actions">
    Right-click this sample card
  </ContextMenuTrigger>
  <ContextMenuContent>
    <ContextMenuGroup>
      <ContextMenuLabel>Example actions</ContextMenuLabel>
      <ContextMenuItem onClick={open}>
        Open<ContextMenuShortcut>Enter</ContextMenuShortcut>
      </ContextMenuItem>
      <ContextMenuItem disabled>Unavailable</ContextMenuItem>
    </ContextMenuGroup>
    <ContextMenuSeparator />
    <ContextMenuItem variant="destructive" onClick={remove}>
      Delete sample
    </ContextMenuItem>
  </ContextMenuContent>
</ContextMenu>`}
    />
    <p>
      <code>ContextMenuTrigger</code> renders a <code>div</code> that wraps the target. Pass <code>render</code> to use
      another element. Give it <code>tabIndex={'{0}'}</code>, a role, and an <code>aria-label</code> when people should
      reach it with the keyboard.
    </p>
  </section>
  <section class="prose-section">
    <h2 class="section-title">Keyboard access</h2>
    <p>
      Right-click and long-press have no keyboard equivalent, so always offer the same actions another way. The items
      are plain Base UI menu parts, so the same elements work inside <code>DropdownMenuContent</code>. Open that menu
      with <code>open</code> and <code>onOpenChange</code> when the focused target receives Shift + F10 or the Menu key,
      and use <code>finalFocus</code> to return focus to the target.
    </p>
    <CodeBlock
      lang="tsx"
      title="Shared items with a keyboard fallback"
      code={`const items = <>{/* ContextMenuItem, ContextMenuSub, … */}</>;

<ContextMenu>
  <ContextMenuTrigger
    tabIndex={0}
    role="group"
    aria-label="Sample card actions"
    onKeyDown={(event) => {
      if ((event.shiftKey && event.key === "F10") || event.key === "ContextMenu") {
        event.preventDefault();
        returnFocus.current = event.currentTarget;
        setOpen(true);
      }
    }}
  >
    Right-click this sample card
  </ContextMenuTrigger>
  <ContextMenuContent>{items}</ContextMenuContent>
</ContextMenu>
<DropdownMenu open={open} onOpenChange={setOpen}>
  <DropdownMenuTrigger render={<Button variant="outline" />}>Open sample actions</DropdownMenuTrigger>
  <DropdownMenuContent size="menu" finalFocus={() => returnFocus.current ?? true}>
    {items}
  </DropdownMenuContent>
</DropdownMenu>`}
    />
  </section>
  <section class="prose-section">
    <h2 class="section-title">Variants and states</h2>
    <p>
      <code>ContextMenuItem variant</code> is <code>"default"</code> or <code>"destructive"</code>; destructive items
      use the danger color and a tinted highlight. Items with a leading icon line up with labels and items that set{' '}
      <code>inset</code>. <code>disabled</code> items stay readable at half opacity and can still be reached with arrow
      keys. While a row syncs, disable the actions that would change it and keep the rest.
    </p>
    <ContextMenuFiles client:load />
  </section>
  <section class="prose-section">
    <h2 class="section-title">Checkboxes and radios</h2>
    <p>
      <code>ContextMenuCheckboxItem</code> and <code>ContextMenuRadioItem</code> show a check on the right. Checkboxes
      keep the menu open; pass <code>closeOnClick</code> to close after one choice. Disable the last visible column so
      the table never goes empty. <code>ContextMenuSub</code> nests a menu: <code>ContextMenuSubTrigger</code> adds a
      chevron and opens <code>ContextMenuSubContent</code> to the side.
    </p>
    <ContextMenuColumns client:load />
  </section>
  <section class="prose-section" id="context-menu-api">
    <h2 class="section-title">API</h2>
    <p>
      <code>ContextMenu</code>, <code>ContextMenuTrigger</code>, <code>ContextMenuPortal</code>,{' '}
      <code>ContextMenuGroup</code>, <code>ContextMenuSub</code>, <code>ContextMenuRadioGroup</code>, and{' '}
      <code>ContextMenuSeparator</code> wrap the Base UI context menu parts and take their props, including{' '}
      <code>open</code>, <code>onOpenChange</code>, and <code>render</code>.
    </p>
    <p>
      <code>ContextMenuContent</code> renders its own portal and positioner. It opens beside the pointer and takes{' '}
      <code>side</code> (<code>"right"</code>), <code>align</code> (<code>"start"</code>), <code>sideOffset</code> (0),
      <code>alignOffset</code> (4), <code>collisionPadding</code> (8), <code>container</code>, and every Base UI popup
      prop. It is at least 9rem wide and grows with its items. <code>ContextMenuSubContent</code> takes the same props.
    </p>
    <p>
      <code>ContextMenuItem</code> takes <code>variant</code> and <code>inset</code>. <code>ContextMenuLabel</code>,{' '}
      <code>ContextMenuSubTrigger</code>, and the checkbox and radio items take <code>inset</code> too. Put a
      <code>ContextMenuLabel</code> inside a <code>ContextMenuGroup</code>; the group takes its name from the label.{' '}
      <code>ContextMenuShortcut</code> is a plain
      <code>span</code> for hint text; it does not bind keys. Every part sets a <code>data-slot</code>.
    </p>
  </section>
  <section class="prose-section">
    <h2 class="section-title">Accessibility</h2>
    <p>
      The popup has <code>role="menu"</code>. Arrow keys move, typing jumps to a matching item, Arrow Right opens a
      submenu and Arrow Left closes it, and Escape closes the menu. A long press opens it on touch screens, and the
      trigger turns off text selection and the system callout so the press isn’t interrupted. A focused trigger shows a
      focus ring.
    </p>
    <p>
      Menus fade and scale in over 120ms. Motion turns off when reduced motion is requested. In forced-colors mode the
      highlighted item gets an outline.
    </p>
  </section>
  <section class="prose-section">
    <h2 class="section-title">Theme tokens</h2>
    <p>
      Menus use <code>--sprout-surface</code>, <code>--sprout-line</code>, <code>--sprout-hover</code>,{' '}
      <code>--sprout-text</code>, <code>--sprout-muted</code>, <code>--sprout-danger</code>,{' '}
      <code>--sprout-danger-subtle</code>, <code>--sprout-focus</code>, <code>--sprout-shadow-overlay</code>, and the
      panel and control radii. They need no brand color, so they look the same with the neutral and TulipFarm themes in
      light and dark mode.
    </p>
  </section>
</Docs>
